  data: {
    LLM: "Don't play 'natural' hands (like Two Pair) past the 5th street. In Low Hole, 'natural' hands usually lose to straights or flushes powered by wild cards.\n\nThe 'Hidden' Wild: If your low hole card is an Ace (and you haven't caught a 2-K in the hole), you have NO wild cards (since Ace is high). However, if your up-cards are all high, opponents might fear you have a small wild. Use this 'phantom wild' to bluff.\n\nHole Card Management: If your first two hole cards are a 2 and a King, your 2s are wild. If you catch another 2 as an up-card, you have a massive advantage. If you catch a 2 as your LAST hole card, your wild hasn't changed, but you now have two natural wild cards.",
    Player: "Don't play 'natural' hands (like Two Pair) past the 5th street. In Low Hole, 'natural' hands usually lose to straights or flushes powered by wild cards.\n\nThe 'Hidden' Wild: If your low hole card is an Ace (and you haven't caught a 2-K in the hole), you have NO wild cards (since Ace is high). However, if your up-cards are all high, opponents might fear you have a small wild. Use this 'phantom wild' to bluff.\n\nHole Card Management: If your first two hole cards are a 2 and a King, your 2s are wild. If you catch another 2 as an up-card, you have a massive advantage. If you catch a 2 as your LAST hole card, your wild hasn't changed, but you now have two natural wild cards.",
