    basic: "Don't play 'natural' hands (like Two Pair) past the 5th street. In Low Hole, 'natural' hands usually lose to straights or flushes powered by wild cards.",
    intermediate: "The 'Hidden' Wild: If your low hole card is an Ace (and you haven't caught a 2-K in the hole), you have NO wild cards (since Ace is high). However, if your up-cards are all high, opponents might fear you have a small wild. Use this 'phantom wild' to bluff.",
    advanced: "Hole Card Management: If your first two hole cards are a 2 and a King, your 2s are wild. If you catch another 2 as an up-card, you have a massive advantage. If you catch a 2 as your LAST hole card, your wild hasn't changed, but you now have two natural wild cards.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Watch the board. If four 7s are already showing as up-cards for other players, and your hole low is a 7, you have a very weak hand because all the 'wild' cards are already accounted for.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'The best starting hand is a pair of low cards in the hole (e.g., ). One is naturally wild, and it makes every 2 you catch a guaranteed wild.',
      },
